A||||10||AkursedX||Can someone tell me what happened with my car?!?||||1||
Z||000000||AkursedX||07-05-2001||01:34 AM||||Ok, well as I posted before, my accel ignition coil went out on me yesterday, so I put my old one back in (it was working fine when i took it out)  <BR>Well I wen out and drove around that night and it ran great!  Then I took it to Burlington Ontario this morning so I could meet up with Grinthock to go to Canada's Wonderland.  It ran great the entire trip up!<P>So..now, I am on my way home.  I am driving along at about 80-85, and all of a sudden, my RPM gauge drops to zero!  WTF  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">  So I immeditately thought my coil went again, BUT, when my coil went before, everything shut down, my check engine light came on, my oil pressure and volt gauge both read zero, and the car was basically dead.<P>So what makes this so weird is that just my RPM gauge dropped to zero, I still had oil pressure, I still had voltage, no check engine light.  And I'm not sure, because I didn't step on the gas, but i think i still had power!<P>So I let myself cruise over to the shoulder of the road, and after about 15 seconds or so of cruising, the RPM guage jumps back up to where it should be!  I pull over anyways to check everything, and it all seemed fine, so I just took it easy and cruised the 60 miles back home.  <P>The only problem I encountered was that it hesitated going uphill when i tried to give it more gas.  <P>So does anyone have any idea what might of happened??  My thoughts were something to do with the tach filter, but I don't know if that would be a symptom or not.<P>Any feedback is GREATLY appreciated.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||tgowens||07-05-2001||01:40 AM||||more than likely you have a clogged catalytic converter........that would be my first assumption.||||reg||1
Z||000002||AkursedX||07-05-2001||01:51 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by tgowens:<BR><B>more than likely you have a clogged catalytic converter........that would be my first assumption.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Highly doubtful....I just had it changed last year, or about 10k ago.  But, I definietly won't count it out.  But would that explain the RPM guage?<P>Actually, I should check my air filter, I haven't done that once since I put the car back on the road now that I think of it (stupid me)  <P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Mach10||07-05-2001||02:31 AM||||Overheating/fried tach filter? Loose connection on the tach wire? Has to be electrical.||||reg||7
Z||000004||tgowens||07-05-2001||05:19 AM||||you might also check the two connections on the top of the coil to see if they have come loose..........||||reg||1
Z||000005||Indiana_resto_guy||07-05-2001||09:23 AM||||It didn't die, right?<BR>Check connections and filter, no worries.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Tom88gt||07-05-2001||09:31 AM||||could be the coil.  the stock ones can do these kinda things as they go bad.  I've had 2 go out in the past 2 years.  Very similar symptoms.  I would recommend always carrying a spare coil.||||reg||1
Z||000007||AkursedX||07-05-2001||01:54 PM||||Can somebody tell me where the tach filter is located?  And Rodney Dickman sells a replacement right?<P>And yes, i am buying a new coil today, and keeping the spare one in my car.  ||||reg||1
Z||000008||87GTZ34||07-06-2001||12:41 AM||||Should be mounted on the bracket that holds the coil.  The original looks like a 'condenser' from a points distributer except is has a wire on each end instead of just one end.  Rodney's looks much different kind of like srink-wrap.  I have his and it works just fine.  It doesn't even fail when I rev it up to 10K. Just kidding.  Seeing if you are awake or not.||||reg||1
Z||000009||88CoupeV6||07-06-2001||11:24 AM||||How about your ignition module?<P>------------------<BR>Josh <B>(known by TheFiero64 for first 1239 posts)</B><BR>     <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg">    <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||5
Z||000010||286SE'S||07-06-2001||03:05 PM||||I had my ignition module fail twice. Both times the tach was dead. I always carry a spare now.||||reg||1
